# MakerPeek — Project Rules

## Product
MakerPeek is a Chrome extension (Manifest V3) that surfaces real sales estimates, POD-supplier detection, base-product analysis, niche/theme extraction, margin estimation, and design velocity on competitor Shopify stores. Targets POD-focused Shopify sellers. Pricing: $14/mo or $129/yr, single tier.

## Stack
- Chrome Extension: Manifest V3, vanilla JS in content scripts (no React), TypeScript where possible
- Backend: Next.js 15 (App Router) on Vercel
- Database: Supabase (Postgres + Auth via magic link)
- Payments: Stripe Checkout (monthly + annual)
- Data: Public Shopify /products.json endpoint, fetched per-request (no bulk pre-scraping)
- AI: Anthropic Claude API (Sonnet 4.6) for niche/theme extraction, only on paid tier
- Scraping infrastructure: Apify Etsy actor NOT needed — use direct fetch to Shopify /products.json

## Conventions
- TypeScript strict mode everywhere
- API routes in /app/api/[...]/route.ts (Next.js App Router)
- Extension code in /extension/ (content scripts, background worker, popup)
- Shared types in /shared/types.ts
- No ENV secrets in client code, ever
- All Claude API calls go through backend, never the extension

## Constraints
- Rate limit Shopify /products.json calls to <40/min per store per IP
- Free tier: 5 lookups/day, by IP + extension fingerprint, no signup
- Paid tier: unlimited lookups, AI features unlocked
- Never cache Shopify product data server-side beyond 24 hours (be respectful of public endpoint)
- Inventory quantity is NOT available publicly — only boolean `available` per variant
- Pricing locked at $14/mo, $129/yr; no feature reshuffling later

## Voice for User-Facing Copy
Direct, no fluff, no preamble. Match the landing page tone (forest green/cream palette, Fraunces + Inter typography). Honest pricing as a brand promise.

## Out of Scope for v1
- Own-shop OAuth integration
- Multi-marketplace support (Etsy, Amazon, etc.)
- Mobile / Firefox / Safari
- Team accounts
